<title>LEBANON: Kuwaiti fund lends Lebanon $33 million for water.</title>
<headline>Kuwaiti fund lends Lebanon $33 million for water.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kuwaiti Fund for Arab Development on Wednesday initialled an agreement with the Lebanese government to lend it 10 million Kuwaiti dinars ($33 million) to finance water projects in Beirut.</p>
<p>The Lebanese government's reconstruction agency, the Council for Development and Reconstruction, said in a statement that the loan was initialled by officials of the CDR and the Kuwaiti Fund.</p>
<p>The loan, which carries a 2.5 percent annual interest rate, has a duration of 25 years, including a five-year grace period.</p>
<p>It brought to 60 million Kuwaiti dinars ($200 million) the total sum of soft loans given by the fund to Lebanon to finance electricity, communications, transportation and water projects, the CDR said. ($1=0.299 dinar)</p>
</text>
